---
to: ".terraform-validate-receipts/{{ moduleName }}.txt"
skip_empty: false
unless_exists: true
for_each: results
sparql:
  results: |
    PREFIX xar: <https://ggen.io/ontology/xaas-ash-render#>
    SELECT ?moduleName ?domainModule WHERE {
      ?t a xar:RenderTarget ;
         xar:moduleName ?moduleName ;
         xar:domainModule ?domainModule .
    }
sh_after: "terraform -chdir=modules/integrations/github/project_management fmt -check -diff 2>&1 | tee -a .terraform-validate-receipts/{{ moduleName }}.tf.log; terraform -chdir=modules/integrations/github/project_management validate 2>&1 | tee -a .terraform-validate-receipts/{{ moduleName }}.tf.log"
---
real terraform fmt -check / validate invocation, driven by the live xar:RenderTarget
ontology row {{ moduleName }} (same SPARQL -> for_each -> sh_after pattern already
proven for Ash codegen in templates-hooks/ash-gen-resource.txt.tmpl), scoped to
modules/integrations/github/project_management/.
generated: {{ moduleName }}
domain: {{ domainModule }}
command: terraform -chdir=modules/integrations/github/project_management fmt -check -diff
command: terraform -chdir=modules/integrations/github/project_management validate

Deliberately non-mutating: `fmt -check` and `validate` only read/lint the real
.tf files under that module -- no `terraform apply`/`plan` against live state,
since apply would create real GitHub resources unpredictably from a research task.

Future scope (not implemented here, not fabricated): a real ggen ontology
vocabulary for Terraform resource individuals (analogous to xar:RenderTarget
for Ash resources) that would let SPARQL rows drive actual .tf resource-block
generation via a templated body, not just fmt/validate of hand-written .tf.
No such vocabulary exists in ontology.ttl today.
